<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Ba Vi by Motorbike: Route Planning | Hanoi Motorbike Guide</h1>
<p>Ba Vi is the mountain massif that stands west of Hanoi, a national park of forested ridges and sacred summits that has been the city&rsquo;s weekend escape for generations, and riding there by motorbike is one of the classic trips a renter can take. Route planning for the ride is less about a single line on a map and more about understanding what the journey contains, the city exit, the plain, the foothills and the climb, and about verifying the few facts that change month to month before the wheels move at all.</p>
<p>The machine for the ride can come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk hands over bikes for western trips every week and answers the planning questions this guide keeps raising. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, read the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/hanoi-to-ba-vi-motorbike-route/">Ba Vi route guide</a>, see the fleet and the terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">What Ba Vi Is</a></li>
